{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7669630","formula":"C₁₁H₁₄BrNO₂","hill":"C11H14BrNO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":14.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"TCB-2"},"descriptions":{"en":"TCB-2, also known as 2CBCB or 2C-BCB, is a putative psychedelic drug of the phenethylamine, 2C, and benzocyclobutene families related to 2C-B. It is a cyclized phenethylamine and is the derivative of 2C-B in which the β position has been connected to the 6 position by a methylene bridge to form a benzocyclobutene ring system. It is unclear whether TCB-2 produces hallucinogenic effects in humans and its route of administration and properties such as dose and duration are unknown. The drug is a highly potent serotonin receptor agonist, including of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor among others."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":16086382,"mass":272.14,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=C(C2=C1[C@@H](C2)CN)OC)Br","inchikey":"MPBCKKVERDTCEL-LURJTMIESA-N","iupac":"[(7R)-3-bromo-2,5-dimethoxy-7-bicyclo[4.2.0]octa-1(6),2,4-trienyl]methanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"16086382","atoms":29,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.827,"y":-0.792,"z":0.255,"el":"Br"},{"x":1.111,"y":-2.535,"z":-0.042,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.244,"y":1.874,"z":-0.241,"el":"O"},{"x":4.105,"y":1.429,"z":0.399,"el":"N"},{"x":1.978,"y":0.623,"z":-0.526,"el":"C"},{"x":1.023,"y":1.862,"z":-0.582,"el":"C"},{"x":0.743,"y":-0.197,"z":-0.295,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.095,"y":0.891,"z":-0.344,"el":"C"},{"x":2.928,"y":0.602,"z":0.649,"el":"C"},{"x":0.273,"y":-1.472,"z":-0.087,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.456,"y":0.772,"z":-0.187,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.106,"y":-1.627,"z":0.076,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.965,"y":-0.511,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":0.529,"y":-3.822,"z":0.18,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.998,"y":2.902,"z":0.721,"el":"C"},{"x":2.476